E=/home/user/Nicole-projects/elevenlabs/el.py
ST="Stylized 3D cartoon animation like a family animated feature film, vertical 9:16, smooth expressive character animation, consistent characters exactly as in the first frame. The macaw keeps the same beige bucket hat with its patch facing forward. The stone statues look like carved stone that moves magically, with small dust particles when they move. One continuous shot, no cuts, no text on screen. Only the character who is speaking moves its mouth; everyone else keeps the mouth closed while listening. Dialogue in Spanish with a Honduran accent. Say ONLY the quoted words, no extra words."
NEG="realistic, photorealistic, text, letters, subtitles, captions, watermark, distorted face, extra limbs, wrong character speaking, lip movement on listeners, extra dialogue, gibberish, morphing objects, camera cuts, flicker"
v(){ o=$1; d=$2; s=$3; p=$4; [ -s p1/vid/$o.mp4 ] && return; python3 $E video "$ST $p" -o p1/vid/$o.mp4 --ar 9:16 --dur $d --res 4K --start p1/sf/$s.png --neg "$NEG" > p1/vid/$o.log 2>&1; }
mkdir -p p1/vid
b1(){
v 01 8 01 "The bored boy lying on the bed stares at the ceiling and complains, lips moving: \"¿Y qué tiene de interesante un montón de piedras viejas?\" The macaw on the window sill listens with its beak closed, then grins and says, beak moving: \"¿Piedras? Agarrá la mochila, cipote... nos vamos a Copán.\" The boy sits up, curious, mouth closed. Ambient: afternoon birds." &
v 02 6 02 "The macaw flies up happily toward the three wild scarlet macaws in the tree and says excitedly, beak moving: \"¡Primas! ¡Ya llegó la familia!\" The wild macaws squawk and flap; the boy below laughs with his mouth closed. Ambient: jungle birds." &
v 03 8 03 "The bored boy looks at the stone statue and says flatly, lips moving: \"Ajá... puras piedras.\" Then the golden sunbeam hits the statue: cracks of golden light, dust falls, the stone king blinks, stretches and looks down at the boy with a grin, saying majestically, his stone mouth moving: \"¿Piedras? ¡Soy Waxaklajuun Ub'aah K'awiil, decimotercer rey de Copán!\" The boy jumps back scared with mouth open in shock. Sound: stone cracking, magical shimmer." &
v 04a 6 04 "The boy hiding behind the macaw peeks out and asks confused, lips moving: \"¿Waxa... qué?\" Then the macaw tries to pronounce it, beak moving, tongue-twisted: \"Wa... Waxa... Waxaklaju... ¡ay, se me trabó el pico!\" and shakes its head dizzy. The stone king above listens smiling with mouth closed." &
wait; }
b2(){
v 04b 6 04 "The giant stone king laughs warmly, bends down to the boy and the macaw and says, his stone mouth moving: \"Me pueden decir Dieciocho Conejo. Vengan, les enseño mi reino.\" and gestures with his stone hand inviting them. The boy and the macaw smile with mouths closed. Sound: stone rumble." &
v 05 8 05 "The stone king points at the carved altar and explains proudly, his stone mouth moving: \"Aquí están los dieciséis reyes de Copán. El primero fundó la ciudad en el año cuatrocientos veintiséis.\" The tiny carved figures on the altar blink one by one with a golden glow. Then the boy says amazed, lips moving: \"¡Hace como mil seiscientos años!\" while the king nods with mouth closed. Ambient: dusk insects." &
v 06 8 06 "The two stone macaw heads on the wall come alive and squawk happily together, beaks moving: \"¡Bienvenida, prima!\" The cartoon macaw below gasps, moved, and asks, beak moving: \"¿Ustedes... son mis tatarabuelas?\" Then the stone king behind says warmly, stone mouth moving: \"La guacamaya era sagrada para nosotros. Por eso cuidan la cancha.\" Ambient: dusk." &
v 07 8 07 "The stone king shouts encouragingly, stone mouth moving: \"¡Con la cadera, no con las manos!\" The boy hits the heavy rubber ball with his hip, almost falls, recovers and the ball flies up through a carved stone ring; he jumps celebrating and shouts, lips moving: \"¡Gooool... digo, punto!\" The stone macaw heads and the cartoon macaw cheer. Sound: ball thud, cheering." &
v 08 6 08 "Blue hour. The glyphs on the stairway glow softly. The small stone scribe on the step slowly turns his head toward the boy and the macaw, raises his brush and says in a mysterious whisper, his stone mouth moving: \"Y eso no es nada... ¿quieren ver un secreto?\" The boy and the macaw look at each other amazed, mouths closed. Sound: magical shimmer." &
wait; }
